    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "description": "How to read this dashboard.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n**What it is.** `llama` (namespace `llm`) runs the llama.cpp server with the **Vulkan** backend on the only GPU (GeForce GT 740,\n4 GiB, Kepler) and serves an **OpenAI-compatible API** at `https://llm.staffops.space` (API key from Vault `homelab/llm`).\nModel: Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct Q4_K_M, context `-c 4096`. Validated speed: ~21 tok/s prompt, **~7.5 tok/s generation**.\n\n**Healthy looks like:** *Up* = UP, *Ready* = 1, *Deferred* = 0, generation speed close to ~7.5 tok/s while requests run, Gateway\nresponses 2xx. When nobody calls the API every rate is 0 and the per-scrape speed gauges sit at 0: that is normal.\n\n**When something goes red:**\n- *Up* DOWN / *Ready* 0 → `kubectl --context k8s01 -n llm get pods,events`; the pod needs the GPU (`nvidia.com/gpu: 1`) and the\n  `nvidia` RuntimeClass — check the **GPU** dashboard (device plugin, VRAM).\n- *Deferred* > 0 → all slots are busy, new requests wait. Expected for bursts on this tiny GPU; sustained = too much load.\n- Generation speed far below ~7.5 tok/s → the model may be running partly on CPU (VRAM full, see VRAM panel) or the GPU is hot.\n- Gateway 5xx / 503 → the pod is not ready or crashed; 401 → wrong/missing API key at the client.\n\nMetric reference: [llama.cpp server README](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/tools/server/README.md#get-metrics-prometheus-compatible-metrics-exporter). Panel descriptions name the source of every formula.\n"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      },
      "id": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Up (scrape)",
      "description": "Prometheus can scrape /metrics of the llama pod (bearer = API key). DOWN means the pod is gone, not ready, or the API key in the ServiceMonitor secret is wrong (scrape gets 401). kube-prometheus-stack alert TargetDown covers it.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(up{job=\"llama\"})",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
